    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="1343" n="1331" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg1331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to Mr. Walter S. Robertson, at
                        Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-09">9 July 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1084. Orders to field forces is subject, 1062 and 1077<anchor n="97"
                        xml:id="d657-f1"/> refers. I learned from General Chou this afternoon that
                    Chairman Mao reiterated June 7th orders to all Communist commanders in Manchuria
                    and China on 1 July 1946.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
